 2: Replaced the undersized handle arch with a source-traced planar centerline, added its raised crest and two attachments, and checked the common geometry in three cameras.\n- Round 2: Baked broad front tarnish boundaries from source annotations; generated pattern is restricted to unseen coverage, with smoother nominal conductor reflectance and separate roughness.\n- Added three calibrated evidence views, source-only manual masks, numeric IoU and masked RGB histogram comparisons.\n- Added physics mass/density/friction/restitution/COM/fragility metadata with uncertainty and synchronized native rigid bodies.\n\nRemaining:\n- Front tarnish uses approximate source-region boundaries; reflected-room separation, fine cast engraving and hidden foot count remain uncertain. Generated material supplies the unobserved back.\n- Product identity and actual weighed mass are unverified; physics parameters are explicitly estimated.\n- External scene integration: the separate cabinetry support differs from this photo-fitted base by +15.1 mm. Its assumed shelf elevation needs reconciliation; cookware was not moved off its source fit. See review/support_reconciliation.json.\n\nMass is an engineering prior, not the real product weight. `physics` includes the shell-area check, density, 40% mass uncertainty, per-body COM and contact coefficients. No deformable item is present in this set.\n\nPer-view bounding dimensions and three projected width samples are measured in source pixels. Rim wall thickness, hidden hinge internals and unreadable markings cannot be resolved to physical accuracy from these images; nominal values are not photo measurements.\n\nPrevious notes are archived in `../review/before/utensil_pitcher/notes.md`; current geometry, poses and physical properties are authoritative in `model.json`. GLB contains visuals; load the JSON joints/collision mapping for simulation.\n\n## Round 2\n\n- Round 2: replaced smooth procedural tarnish with a reference-conditioned PBR texture e